{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/392598-researching-history-or-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-washington-state","id":392598,"title":"Researching History OR A Werewolf Chronicle in Washington State","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-04T08:03:04-08:00","id":392598,"title":"Researching History OR A Werewolf Chronicle in Washington State","content":"All this Dark Eras stuff has me in the mood to run a historical game. But I need some help with the<br /> <br /> I didn't do a lot of extra research into Seattle or the 1980s beyond reading the <i>New Wave Requiem</i> book. While my players and I have had a good time, I feel like there wasn't anything particularly <i>80s</i> or <i>Seattle</i> about the game other than me occasionally referencing how hopped up on coffee the Kine were or reminding the players that they didn't have cell phones.<br /> <br /> Why did I pick it originally? It was kind of on a lark, and I had just started playing in a friend's Shadowrun game, and I wanted to emphasize Seattle's isolation. Why the 80s? I was going through an 80s music kick at the time, and wanted an excuse to use exclusively 80s music in a game. Which is all well and good, but I want something a little less shallow next time, yanno?<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Which brings me to my point: Once Werewolf 2E finally drops, I'm moving my campaign forward to the 1990s, switching to werewolf, and opening up the Pacific Northwest as a sandbox. Something I want to do now is make it <i>feel</i> like it belongs there. I have a <i>why</i> this time, but still no experience. Other than watching <i>Twin Peaks</i>, I'm not sure how to prepare for this. Anybody have advice for doing first-hand research into unfamiliar real-world settings?<br /> <br /> Summary<br /> <br /> <b>Theme:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Counter-Culture </b>- In the human society, Seattle is the birthplace of Grunge, and in the 1990s it had spread like wildfire across the nation. Even though Kurt Cobain is dead, the genre is doing better than ever on the charts. The population of the Pacific Northwest in both the United States and Canada is beginning to form around the embryonic Cascadian movement, and the rumor of &quot;secession&quot; is beginning to spread. Mirroring this trend in Uratha society, disaffected youths in both Pure and Forsaken packs demand recognition and question the old ways. Potentially noble, the fact remains that darker elements will seek to corrupt and suborn this movement for their own purposes.<br /> <br /> <b>Mood:</b><br /> <br /> <b>A Secret War</b> - America in the 90s was breathing peacefully for the first time in 70 years. Depression, a World War, and a Cold War with Russia had brought the country nearly to its breaking point, but it managed to make it through those trying times intact. Americans have prepared to enter an era of peace and prosperity. The Forsaken have no such reprieve. Their war against the Pure has taken a turn for the worse, and very few Forsaken packs remain in the Cascadian region. The peaceful status quo of the humans makes this war much harder to hide, however, as there are no convenient scapegoats to point to when the bodies start to pile up. Even the Shadow hasn't gotten the memo yet that the Cold War is over yet. America's social troubles from the 70s and 80s created paranoia, racial and sexual tension, and conformity spirit courts that continue to thrive.<br /> <br /> Since I know I start a lot of these &quot;Help me be a Storyteller&quot; threads, I want to go ahead and thank ya'll for the positive responses I've gotten in the past, and hopefully will get again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T09:11:56-08:00","id":392641,"title":"","content":"I tend to read books and watch shows or movies. The problem with tv and movies though is that they tend to be skewed, biased or just plain wrong. Not that books are fonts of Absolute Truth. Either way, if you're not concerned with portraying 100% reality even taking from over or under glamorized sources can help build up an atmosphere. I suppose the 90s would be at least easier having grown up in them, though on the completely opposite side of the country. It looks like <a href=\"http://www.reddit.com/r/Seattle/comments/1aqzeg/how_was_seattle_different_in_the_90s/\" target=\"_blank\">reddit</a> might be a good resource.<br /> <br /> Now that I think of it, this is the New World of Darkness forum, and right next to us is the Classic World of Darkness forum. I'm sure the classic World of Darkness books had something on Seattle, I know at least some of the fiction took place there. Obviously the supernatural aspects would have to change but surely some book would tell you about the mundane climate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-04-2015, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T12:43:56-08:00","id":402263,"title":"","content":"I was born, raised and still live about 40 miles south of Seattle (still north-ish of Tacoma though). I was born in the mid-eighties so my 90's knowledge will skew to a certain point of view. But i Would be glad to provide some insight into the area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}